{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1036","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Relatively Prime Powers"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider some positive integer $$$x$$$. Its prime factorization will be of form $$$x = 2^{k_1} \\cdot 3^{k_2} \\cdot 5^{k_3} \\cdot \\dots$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's call $$$x$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"elegant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the greatest common divisor of the sequence $$$k_1, k_2, \\dots$$$ is equal to $$$1$$$. For example, numbers $$$5 = 5^1$$$, $$$12 = 2^2 \\cdot 3$$$, $$$72 = 2^3 \\cdot 3^2$$$ are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"elegant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and numbers $$$8 = 2^3$$$ ($$$GCD = 3$$$), $$$2500 = 2^2 \\cdot 5^4$$$ ($$$GCD = 2$$$) are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Count the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"elegant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers from $$$2$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each testcase contains several values of $$$n$$$, for each of them you are required to solve the problem separately."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$T$$$ ($$$1 \\le T \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of values of $$$n$$$ in the testcase."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$T$$$ lines contains a single integer $$$n_i$$$ ($$$2 \\le n_i \\le 10^{18}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$T$$$ lines — the $$$i$$$-th line should contain the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"elegant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers from $$$2$$$ to $$$n_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n4\n2\n72\n10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n1\n61\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here is the list of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-elegant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers up to $$$10$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$4 = 2^2, GCD = 2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$8 = 2^3, GCD = 3$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$9 = 3^2, GCD = 2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The rest have $$$GCD = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1036F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1036/problem/F"}